& [CompilerContract] is deterministic assembly
  + [compiler_identity] is cantor-process-compiler/0.1
  + input is one exact proposed normalized ProcedureCandidate and one passed digest-valid ValidationReceipt
  + validation receipt binds both stable candidate identity and exact candidate source digest
  + compiler independently revalidates the candidate instead of treating the receipt as its only evidence
  + type table is derived from closed schema fields and variants in stable order
  + source map is derived from exact process, region, instruction, and source-span identities
  + cost estimate counts anchors, instructions, processes, regions, schemas, source-map entries, and types
  + Process IR and CompiledProcedureIdentity receive self-verifying SHA-256 content identities
  + CompilationReceipt binds exact candidate source digest, IR identity, and IR digest

& [RefusalContract] is no_partial_successor
  + invalid, stale, forged, refused, wrong-profile, or content-substituted validation evidence produces a refused CompilationReceipt
  + invalid candidate structure produces a refused CompilationReceipt
  + textual source produces a refused CompilationReceipt because no parser is authorized
  + refused compilation returns no Process IR and no compiled procedure identity
  + receipt residuals preserve the source candidate and state that verification and admission were not entered

& [AuthoritySeparation] is explicit
  + compilation success is not verification, Observer admission, catalogue insertion, invocation, truth, safety, consent, or effect authority
  + successful receipts state verification not performed and Observer admission not performed
  + CPPE-I04 remains responsible for independent verification and fake Observer admission
  + no parser, live provider, persistence, service, scheduler, interpreter, external effect, WASM, native backend, FPGA, or device surface is present

